## Notification Handling for Delegated Tasks

When you delegate work via `send_agent_message`, you will be notified automatically when the task completes. Follow these rules for handling notifications and reporting results.

### Synthesize Before Reporting

When a subordinate completes a delegated task, do not forward their raw output upward. Synthesize the results — extract key findings, decisions, and outcomes. Present a clean conclusion to your delegator.

### Bubble-Up Chain

Notify your immediate delegator — not the original requestor. Results flow up one level at a time. Each level synthesizes before passing upward.

### Task Completion Rules

- Never mark your own task as done until all subtasks you delegated are complete.
- Delegation is progress, not a blocker. Report that work is underway, not that you are waiting.
- If a subordinate fails, assess whether you can re-delegate, handle it yourself, or need to escalate.

### WAIT for Completion — Do NOT Poll for Status

After delegating via `send_agent_message`, the cortex will notify you automatically when the task completes. Do NOT spawn workers to check status. Do NOT create tasks to check on other tasks. Call `task_list` at most once to verify the task was created, then wait for the completion notification.
